":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Plexus Corp. provides electronic manufacturing services in the United States, the Asia-Pacific, Europe, the Middle East, and Africa. The company offers design, develop, supply chain, new product introduction, and manufacturing solutions, as well as sustaining services. It serves the aerospace/defense, healthcare/life sciences, and industrial/commercial sectors. Plexus Corp. was founded in 1979 and is headquartered in Neenah, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Todd P. Kelsey | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25K people. Revenue per employee of $161K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $6K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 19\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Plexus Corp. is a mid-cap technology business with a $5.6B market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 9% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $154M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.44\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 17\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"10,500 Shares of Plexus Corp. $PLXS Acquired by Lisanti Capital Growth LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/10500-shares-of